.TH LIBMPQ__ARCHIVE_VERIFY 3 2026-09-18 "The MoPaQ archive library"
.SH NAME
libmpq__archive_verify \- verify a weak or strong archive signature
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <libmpq/mpq.h>
.sp
.BI "int32_t libmpq__archive_verify("
.BI "        mpq_archive_s *" "archive,"
.BI "        uint32_t " "verify_flags,"
.BI "        const uint8_t *" "public_key,"
.BI "        size_t " "public_key_size,"
.BI "        uint32_t *" "mismatches"
.BI ");"
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
Verifies exactly one signature type selected by \fIverify_flags\fP:
\fBLIBMPQ_SIGNATURE_WEAK\fP or \fBLIBMPQ_SIGNATURE_STRONG\fP. The
caller supplies the matching \fIpublic_key\fP. A cryptographic mismatch
is reported through \fI*mismatches\fP, not as a negative operation error.
A non-NULL mismatch output is zeroed before validation.
.PP
Weak public keys are exactly 128 raw bytes: a 64-byte unsigned
big-endian modulus followed by a zero-padded 64-byte public exponent.
Strong public keys use the same layout with 256-byte fields, 512 bytes
total. The modulus must be full-width and odd; the exponent must be odd,
at least 3, and less than the modulus. No PEM parser or default or
product-specific keys are built in.
.PP
Weak verification uses legacy MD5/RSA-512. Strong verification accepts
the plain SHA-1 archive-range digest as well as the uppercase-basename
and ARCHIVE variants. Internal weak signatures can be verified in
MPQE-wrapped MPQs; no external strong-signature transport is defined for
MPQE. These legacy signatures should not be treated as modern trust
primitives.
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns \fBLIBMPQ_SUCCESS\fP after verification. The requested bit is
set in \fI*mismatches\fP if the signature does not match; it is clear
when it matches. On failure the function returns a negative libmpq error
and leaves a non-NULL mismatch output zero.
.SH ERRORS
An absent requested signature or NULL required argument returns
\fBLIBMPQ_ERROR_EXIST\fP. Invalid flags, key representation, or
signature storage return \fBLIBMPQ_ERROR_FORMAT\fP. Writer handles return
\fBLIBMPQ_ERROR_NOT_INITIALIZED\fP. Read, allocation, and other
lower-level errors may also propagate.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR libmpq (3),
.BR libmpq__archive_signatures (3),
.BR libmpq__archive_sign (3),
.BR libmpq__patch_sign (3)
